Subject: Bug in sqrt test

Nuts!!!

Right after I mailed my note, I saw that I'd forgotten to bump the index 

for the second evaluation in sub4.f.  Doing so causes the performance to 

drop back to the same range as most of the other examples (i.e. 45 cycles).  

So how does Cray get to 25 cycles per result in libm vector and 20 cycles 

in libmfastv vector?

I'd sure like to know and I bet others would too,

Reginald Beardsley

